{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01042",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.25,
      "end_seconds": 5.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "Right, morning, come on through. Have you been waiting long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.0,
      "end_seconds": 14.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Oh, only about ten minutes, no trouble."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.52,
      "end_seconds": 19.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "How are things, what's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.38,
      "end_seconds": 23.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "I'm here because of a severe headache."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.56,
      "end_seconds": 28.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "Has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.16,
      "end_seconds": 38.42,
      "duration_seconds": 9.26,
      "text": "hm it was either the end of last month or earlier than that i couldn't tell you the date"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.59,
      "end_seconds": 43.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "okay, would you say mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.56,
      "end_seconds": 55.81,
      "duration_seconds": 11.25,
      "text": "uh, about a six out of ten. Oh, um, I've also had a rash that does not fade, for about a month"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.23,
      "end_seconds": 61.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "alright, any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.75,
      "end_seconds": 67.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Well, no, nothing as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.28,
      "end_seconds": 89.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.98,
      "end_seconds": 96.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "I'm on lisinopril, 10 milligrams, once a day for my pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.74,
      "end_seconds": 100.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Roughly how long on that one?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.01,
      "end_seconds": 110.23,
      "duration_seconds": 8.22,
      "text": "About a month now it's allopurinol, 100 milligrams, maybe, once a day for the gout"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.11,
      "end_seconds": 116.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "Have you got the box or the prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.63,
      "end_seconds": 120.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it it next time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.56,
      "end_seconds": 124.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "What line of work are you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.74,
      "end_seconds": 132.13,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.82,
      "end_seconds": 136.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Tell me about your eating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.16,
      "end_seconds": 143.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.76,
      "end_seconds": 146.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.24,
      "end_seconds": 152.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.06,
      "end_seconds": 167.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.52,
      "end_seconds": 183.06,
      "duration_seconds": 13.54,
      "text": "sorry, um, what was I saying, I've got high blood pressure. I did try to ignore it for a while. Mm, I have gout, for two years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.19,
      "end_seconds": 193.36,
      "duration_seconds": 9.17,
      "text": "yes okay, I can see high blood pressure and gout in your file as well did you ever have any procedures done?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.15,
      "end_seconds": 199.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Erm, I had my septum straightened in my thirties."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.87,
      "end_seconds": 212.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "right, any cough or recent head injury?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.52,
      "end_seconds": 216.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "no, nothing to report there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.72,
      "end_seconds": 218.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.66,
      "end_seconds": 221.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.26,
      "end_seconds": 226.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Any change in your bowel habit or your stomach generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.14,
      "end_seconds": 229.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.68,
      "end_seconds": 234.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "let me get the readings out of the way"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.73,
      "end_seconds": 248.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "alright, keep your arm relaxed for me.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.22,
      "end_seconds": 273.17,
      "duration_seconds": 7.95,
      "text": "Okay: temperature 39.2, pulse 104, oxygen saturation is 95 percent, blood pressure 109 over 80, respiratory rate 18."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 274.42,
      "end_seconds": 276.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.36,
      "end_seconds": 281.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Don't worry, we'll discuss it it in a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.3,
      "end_seconds": 286.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.36,
      "end_seconds": 289.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.6,
      "end_seconds": 313.34,
      "duration_seconds": 7.74,
      "text": "your neck is stiff, you are feverish, and there are purple spots that do not fade when pressed"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.68,
      "end_seconds": 334.2,
      "duration_seconds": 17.52,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check. Okay, thinking it through, this looks most like possible bacterial meningitis. Let me repeat that back to make sure. You've had a severe headache, and no cough or recent head injury."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 336.21,
      "end_seconds": 338.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Right, that's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.78,
      "end_seconds": 375.21,
      "duration_seconds": 35.43,
      "text": "I want blood cultures done, that's for possible meningitis. I'll request a lumbar puncture, it'll help with possible meningitis. What I'm giving you is benzylpenicillin, 1.2 grams, once now, single dose. It's for possible meningitis. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Call an ambulance now, this is an emergency. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 380.22,
      "end_seconds": 383.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "okay, so thank you, that's clear"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 384.31,
      "end_seconds": 394.66,
      "duration_seconds": 10.35,
      "text": "keep an eye out, and if you cannot go now, call us the same day or go to emergency i'll want another look straight away"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 396.02,
      "end_seconds": 396.72,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 397.93,
      "end_seconds": 400.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 402.2,
      "end_seconds": 405.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "no, that's all thanks a lot"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 407.63,
      "end_seconds": 408.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}